coder v0.0.0-devel

USAGE:
  coder exp api [flags] <path>

  Make an authenticated HTTP request to the Coder API and print the response.

  The path is relative to /api/v2/, with or without a leading slash. Paths that
  start with /api/ are used as given, for example /api/experimental/chats.
  
  Fields are sent as query parameters for GET and HEAD requests or when --input
  is set, and as a JSON object otherwise. The method defaults to GET, or POST
  when fields or --input are provided, so use -X GET to send fields as query
  parameters.
  
  --field (-F) converts true, false, null, and integers to JSON values, and
  reads the value from a file with @path or from stdin with @-. Use
  key[sub]=value for nested objects and key[]=value for arrays. --raw-field (-f)
  always sends strings.
  
  --paginate follows offset and limit pagination until every page is printed.
  Each page is printed as its own JSON document. Use the global --verbose flag
  to print request and response headers to stderr.
  
    - Get the authenticated user:
  
       $ coder exp api users/me
  
    - Print the username of every user:
  
       $ coder exp api users --paginate --jq '.users[].username'
  
    - Create an organization:
  
       $ coder exp api /organizations -f name=new-org -f display_name="New
  Organization"
  
    - Send a JSON body from stdin:
  
       $ echo '{"name":"new-name"}' | coder exp api -X PATCH workspaces/<id>
  --input -

OPTIONS:
  -F, --field string-array
          Add a typed parameter in key=value format. Can be specified multiple
          times.

  -i, --include bool
          Print the response status line and headers before the body.

      --input string
          The file to use as the request body, or - to read from stdin.

  -q, --jq string
          Filter each JSON response with a jq expression. String results are
          printed without quotes.

  -X, --method string
          The HTTP method for the request.

      --paginate bool
          Request every page of results by following offset and limit
          pagination.

  -f, --raw-field string-array
          Add a string parameter in key=value format. Can be specified multiple
          times.

  -H, --request-header string-array
          Add a request header in key:value format. Can be specified multiple
          times.

———
Run `coder --help` for a list of global options.
